      "widgets_values": [
        "## Use your own data\n\n- Replace **Formula Data Generator** with `Read CSV` / `Read XLSX` / `Read DB` — they all output the same teal `DATASET`, so **everything downstream stays unchanged**. Million-row tables are fine.\n- Scale `num_examples` on the generator, or `steps` / `batch_size` on the trainer.\n- **Digital twin:** wire any `nn_model` (e.g. this trainer's `nn_model` output) into the generator's **model** input — it re-simulates fresh data from your trained model, ignoring the formula.\n- Watch the **live loss curve** rendered under the training node while it runs.\n- **Experiment:** the default formula is purely linear, so the trainer converges to the noise floor. Add `+ 0.5*sin(6*x0)` to the formula and watch a *linear* model hit a floor around 0.37 RMSE — then set the trainer's `hidden` widget to `16` and try again."
      ]
    },
